  "fact_notes": [
    "オリジナル教材。一般的な考え方と架空例を用いた文章であり、実在の人物、調査、実験、法令、技術運用手順ではない。制作台帳は来歴確認用。"
  ],
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "id": "p1",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "en": "A girl named Anna found an old notebook in her grandmother's kitchen.",
          "ja": "アンナという少女は祖母の台所で古いノートを見つけた。"
        },
        {
          "en": "Its pages contained recipes written by different people.",
          "ja": "ページには異なる人が書いた料理法があった。"
        },
        {
          "en": "Some of the recipes used words she did not understand.",
          "ja": "一部は理解できない語を使っていた。"
        },
        {
          "en": "She asked her grandmother about the notebook.",
          "ja": "祖母にノートについて尋ねた。"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "en": "Her grandmother explained that neighbors often exchanged recipes many years ago.",
          "ja": "何年も前に近所の人がよく料理法を交換したと祖母は説明した。"
        },
        {
          "en": "They sometimes wrote a friend's name beside a recipe.",
          "ja": "時に料理法の横に友人の名前を書いた。"
        },
        {
          "en": "Anna noticed that one recipe had two different names.",
          "ja": "一つの料理法に二つの異なる名前があると気づいた。"
        },
        {
          "en": "Her grandmother could not remember why both names were there.",
          "ja": "祖母はなぜ両名があるか思い出せなかった。"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p3",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "en": "Anna decided to make a small record of the notebook for her school project.",
          "ja": "学校活動のためノートの小さな記録を作ると決めた。"
        },
        {
          "en": "She copied the recipes and asked about the names.",
          "ja": "料理法を写し名前について質問した。"
        },
        {
          "en": "She wrote down what her grandmother could remember.",
          "ja": "祖母が思い出せることを書き留めた。"
        },
        {
          "en": "She also marked the questions that had no clear answer.",
          "ja": "明確な答えのない問いにも印を付けた。"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p4",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "en": "At school, Anna shared her work with the class.",
          "ja": "学校で作品をクラスに共有した。"
        },
        {
          "en": "Several students had similar notebooks at home.",
          "ja": "何人かの生徒にも家に似たノートがあった。"
        },
        {
          "en": "They began comparing the ways their families had recorded recipes.",
          "ja": "家族が料理法を記録した方法を比較し始めた。"
        },
        {
          "en": "Their teacher reminded them to ask permission before sharing family records.",
          "ja": "教師は家族の記録を共有前に許可を尋ねるよう注意した。"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p5",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "en": "Anna learned that everyday objects can contain stories about the past.",
          "ja": "日常の物にも過去の物語が含まれ得るとアンナは学んだ。"
        },
        {
          "en": "A recipe can tell us more than how to prepare a meal.",
          "ja": "料理法は食事の準備法以上を伝え得る。"
        },
        {
          "en": "It may show how people helped one another.",
          "ja": "人々がどう助け合ったか示すかもしれない。"
        },
        {
          "en": "Even an unanswered question can make an old object interesting.",
          "ja": "未解決の問いでさえ古い物を面白くできる。"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
